      "side": 1,
      "message": "Update; I reproduced your `Test:` and, in my case, `virtmgr` gets properly killed while `crosvm` gets re-parented to `init` (with no `SIGKILL` seemingly delivered).\n\nGiven that [`PR_SET_PDEATHSIG(2const)`](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/PR_SET_PDEATHSIG.2const.html) mentions some cases where the parent-death signal isn\u0027t carried over through the `exec` depending on the payload, I\u0027ve adapted my PoC above to compile for Android (instead of Linux) and use `/apex/.../crosvm` (instead of `sleep`). Running that on my device, I can still reproduce the expected behavior where `crosvm` gets `SIGKILL`-ed when its parent dies so I don\u0027t think the issue is coming from `crosvm` itself.\n\nIn the same way, I\u0027ve also ruled out the issue coming from `SharedChild`.",
